	"identifying_description": "An tent-pole before it has been finished. It shows how an okbash is woven (the starting and ending lines of the weaving forming the side seam of the bag when completed. Along one side of the weaving, triangular sections lacking pile project into reciprocal trianglur forms that are decorated with pile that is continuous with the body of the weaving. To create the bag, the unpiled sections are cut and the sides of adjacent pile trianges sewn togethher to form the closed bottom of the bag.",
